---
code: whylog-unwritten
when-fires: a plan/apply/round-trip run finished but its posthoc-why durable did not land - the whylog directory is unusable, the serializer refused a whole document, the bytes exceeded the retention cap, or the create/write failed. cli/main.rs write seat, over the cli-local hardened store. {dir} and the closed {reason} word.
why: 28D:must-default-durable-lands-with-its-hardening bills a durable for VISIBLE persistence failure; this write path previously answered all five of its failure modes with a bare return, which 28D names among the whylog's each-looked-local decisions. Error-floor rather than advisory (28F:rul-write-failure-is-error-floor) because the advisory plane is suppressed under `apply`, and an apply whose receipt silently vanished is exactly the run an admin later comes back asking about. The artifact on stdout is unaffected - a postmortem aid failing is loud, never fatal. Remediation register (help) wanted: name what to check for the reported reason, and note that the run itself completed and its artifact is unaffected.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork tune --profile web

-- controller-results.txt --
dorc-records/1 nonce=dorc attempt=1 host=localhost book=6b796e0c816aa119a94373a3ab99578a69820f243017ce833973242dd6f9a79e sites=1 @@dorc@@
dorc site 0 effect=holds rc=0 @@dorc@@
dorc-records-end/1 nonce=dorc @@dorc@@

-- edge-fault --
whylog-publish directory

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh --results - --whylog-dir=/var/lib/dorc/whylog < controller-results.txt > /dev/null
probe: note[site-unresolvable]: sm 1 site run unprobed (no read-only check could
be shipped): `hork tune --profile web` -- run `dorc why` for the per-site detail
(the apply runs each anyway, to stay safe)
      [ book.sh:2:1
   2 | hork tune --profile web
     | \_____________________/

   = help:  sm site runs `hork tune --profile web`
hint: 'hork' (line 2) is unmodeled: it is the first wall -- an oracle vouching its convergence would elide it when converged
dorc: run `dorc why` for the per-site cause-chains, or `dorc why book.sh:N` to query a source line
dorc: plan-summary sites=1 elide=0 omit=0 guard=0 run=1 may-alias=0
dorc: decision-digest 06df1751266e3439355f82ea0d81d009679999ffc67b89854dbf6609ebec3eb0
whylog: error[whylog-unwritten]: This run completed and its artifact is
unaffected, but the why-log did not land in /var/lib/dorc/whylog (reason:
directory), so `dorc why --last` will have nothing to read for it.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: whylog-unwritten
{{count}} = "1"
{{site_word}} = "site"
{{v0}} = "book.sh"
{{v1}} = "0"
{{v2}} = "0"
{{v3}} = "0"
{{v4}} = "1"
{{v5}} = "0"
{{dir}} = "/var/lib/dorc/whylog"
{{reason}} = "directory"
